---
description: |
  Normalizes an ISC BIND `named` message record to OCSF 1.9.

  The input record contains the collection timestamp in `time` and the raw
  `named` message body in `message`. One call parses the body, maps the
  structured event to OCSF DNS Activity or Base Event, and preserves the body
  as provenance:

  ```tql
  named::ocsf::normalize
  ```

  Callers that need to inspect or enrich the structured BIND event use
  `named::parse` and `named::ocsf::map` instead.
args:
  positional:
    - name: event
      description: The record carrying `time` and the raw `message` body.
      type: field
      default: this
  named:
    - name: into
      description: The field that receives the OCSF event.
      type: field
      default: this
---

// Stage the carrier fields before writing the output so the default in-place
// call and a distinct nested output follow the same path.
$into = {
  raw_data: $event.message?.string(),
  time: $event.time,
}
named::parse $into.raw_data, $into.named
$into.named.time = move $into.time
named::ocsf::map $into.named, $into.ocsf
$into.raw_data_size = $into.raw_data?.length_bytes()

$into = {
  ...$into.ocsf,
  raw_data: move $into.raw_data,
  raw_data_size: move $into.raw_data_size,
}
